  "semantics": [
    {
      "area": "Export registration",
      "conclusion": "The lowercase name, optional lowercase export alias and conditional default produce exactly the original distinct key set. Computing add_default before filtering the alias preserves default collisions. The file bucket is entered once; each distinct key receives the symbol index once, in original symbol order. Existing map lookups, lifecycle and other indexes are unchanged."
    },
    {
      "area": "Empty and Unicode aliases",
      "conclusion": "Equality uses the same lowercase Strings as the original HashSet. An empty alias remains unless it equals the empty name; default is added only when absent from both keys. Unicode lowercase expansion is unchanged. HashMap key insertion order may change, while each key's rows and exported lookup remain the same."
    },
    {
      "area": "Path distance",
      "conclusion": "The two collected slash-segment Vectors become a streamed zip over the same strip_ext borrowed paths. Empty, repeated and trailing segments, Unicode and case-sensitive extension handling are preserved."
    },
    {
      "area": "Candidate selection",
      "conclusion": "The single pass retains every maximal-distance candidate in input order. Clearing lower maxima preserves the final subset; empty input remains empty. Unmodified stable_candidates retains its exact stable sort and adjacent identity deduplication. No new uniqueness or confidence rule is introduced."
    },
    {
      "area": "Tests and unchanged source",
      "conclusion": "Independently replacing only the three production regions and removing the added reference helpers and four methods restores both original full files exactly. All pre-existing tests and remaining production bytes are preserved. The new reference controls cover collisions, remove/readd, path edge cases and exhaustive candidate sequences."
    },
    {
      "area": "Formatting history",
      "conclusion": "Read the original formatter followup facts and independent review. Final bodies match owner-fixed 69ca and 417e. The earlier format failure 9f345 and all eight historical archive bodies remain unchanged with original source identities. No local formatting, Rust, test or performance execution is claimed."
